SUMMARY:[Machine Learning][Deep Representation Learning] LoG 2026 - Abstrac
 t registration deadline (both tracks)
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: Learning on Graphs Conference\nWebsite: https
 ://logconference.org/\nSource URL: https://logconference.org/cfp/\nLocati
 on: Boston\, Massachusetts\, USA\nTopics: Machine Learning\, Deep Represe
 ntation Learning\, Graphs & Graph Learning\, Learning Theory & Statistica
 l Foundations\nSize: M\nSubmission type: Paper-based / non-archival exten
 ded abstracts\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-10-07\nNote
 s: Fifth annual edition\, in person at Northeastern University. Extended 
 Aug 5/7 deadlines replace the struck-through July 29/Aug 1 dates. Proceed
 ings papers and non-archival extended abstracts share the registration an
 d final submission cutoffs\, represented as one route. The TMLR presentat
 ion track requires an already published paper\, so it is not a new-paper 
 opportunity. LoG is distinct from LOD/AIS. Size M is an editorial estimat
 e.\nScope: Learning on graphs and geometry: graph neural networks\, equiv
 ariant models\, graph kernels\, geometric and graph generative models\, a
 nd statistical theory for structured data. Graph signal processing\, caus
 al graph models\, robustness\, and scalable graph-learning infrastructure
  are meaningful extensions. A graph or geometric contribution should rema
 in central\, even in an application such as language or molecular modelin
 g.\nAdditional topics: Complex Systems & Network Science\, Probabilistic\
 , Causal & Uncertainty ML\, Signal Processing\, Robustness & Safety\, ML 
 Systems & Infrastructure\nScope sources (2026): https://logconference.org
 /cfp/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07
URL:https://logconference.org/cfp/
END:VEVENT
